00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.340
Leah: Communication in business
can be broken down into different

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.350
types such as formal and informal.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.860
Formal communication is the flow of
information through formal channels

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.460
and can be verbal or written.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.639
It is often hierarchical in
nature and controlled by managers.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:21.029
Lines of communication may go down
and up or even horizontally but are

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.600
generally controlled via management
and follow a systematic approach.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.159
Informal communication is based on
personal interactions and relationships.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:33.190
It can be unstructured and unplanned
and does not follow the formal

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.930
channels established by management.

00:00:35.709 --> 00:00:39.160
We all communicate in different ways
at different times whether formally

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.620
or informally so let’s have a look
at these in a little more detail.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.049
Jack: Verbal communication
involves speaking with others.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.960
It may be face-to face, over the telephone
or via digital media and the internet.

00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:54.209
It may also be on a one-to-one
basis or with a group.

00:00:55.049 --> 00:00:59.280
Verbal communication can also be formal
or informal in many different ways from

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.230
presentations, meetings, interviews,
discussions, to one-on-one conversations,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.839
both personal and for business.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.479
Verbal communication can be
impacted by tone and language and

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.730
non-verbal communication elements
and may be backed up by other means

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.360
of communication including visual
imagery or written communication.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:21.990
Leah: Non-verbal communication
includes facial expressions, posture,

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:26.739
eye contact, hand movements and
touch and can be used on its own

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.620
or alongside verbal communication.

00:01:29.309 --> 00:01:33.050
A listener can communicate their response
non-verbally without saying anything.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.850
Non-verbal communication is often used
formally in meetings and interviews

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:42.650
but is also used informally in social
circumstances and personal relationships.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.820
Jack: Written communication can
traditionally be in the form of a letter,

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:53.610
but often now involves emails, texts,
memos, reports, Tweets, contracts etc.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.860
In the short form they should be clear
and concise, but in the long form

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.759
may include more complex information.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.819
However, the speeds and methods of
communication today in the digital

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.300
age, can often lead to poorly spelt and
constructed sentences and careless errors.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.690
Written communication can be used
both formally and informally.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.620
Leah: Visual communication is all
around us from posters and ads on

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.980
a wall, to images on a TV screen.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:24.010
We are bombarded by social media
with visual imagery on sites such as

00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:26.590
Instagram, Facebook, TikTok and YouTube.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.510
It can also be used in conjunction
with written communication and

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.880
verbal communication and often also
involves non-verbal communication.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.329
Visual communication can often be
used to back up verbal communication

00:02:39.339 --> 00:02:43.260
within a formal setting such as
work presentations and advertising,

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.690
but often it is used informally.

